Condition : 22 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:
(a)	any external illumination of the site during construction operations;
(b) 	measures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site during construction operations; 
(c) 	measures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties;
(d)	temporary landscape works along the western (Ealing Road) site boundary; 
(e)	illumination of the interior of buildings prior to their occupation; and
(f)	other measures that would be implemented to regulate the environmental impact of the construction process.
The scheme so approved should be fully implemented on commencement of development (or with respect only to matter (d) in accordance with a timetable agreed in writing with the Local Planning Authority).
Supporting note: 
(a)	In assessing any detail submitted the Council will have regard to the range of measures set out in the Environmental Statement Part 1: Assessment submitted with the application.

Condition : 31 - The play areas shown on Landscape Masterplan 694.L02 Rev F within Courtyards A, B and C shall be laid out in accordance with detailed landscape design proposals that shall have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority prior to the occupation of:
(a)	In respect of Courtyard A, Building 5;
(b)	In respect of Courtyard B, Buildings 6 or 7;
(c)	In respect of Courtyard C, Buildings 9 or 10;
and shall not thereafter be used for any purpose other than as a play area.
